% END SENTENCE r4.fig.world

% SENTENCE r4.world2.01
A reader can start from a claim, locate its declarations, follow the recorded dependencies and request the source lines relevant to a question.
% END SENTENCE r4.world2.01
% SENTENCE r4.world2.02
Declaration locations cover the inventory; dependency edges are exact for selected starts. Interpretations are selective and largely contextual, not records of individual proof review.
% END SENTENCE r4.world2.02
% SENTENCE r4.world2.03
Lookup locates source without recording execution. A Lean check requires a focused build and inspection of its result.
\FloatBarrier
% END SENTENCE r4.world2.03


% SENTENCE r8.architecture.tools
\subsection{Operations on the records}
The entry points below act on the same repository records. They support a research iteration; their order of use is chosen by the researcher or agent.
\begin{center}\small
\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{2.55cm}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}X@{}}
\toprule
Component & Input, output and responsibility\\
\midrule
Task routing & \repolink{scripts/agent_entry.py}{agent\_entry.py} maps a stated task to instructions, relevant files and commands. It routes a request rather than choosing the research question.\\[3pt]
Evidence retrieval & \repolink{scripts/query_corpus.py}{query\_corpus.py} returns problem, claim, declaration and paper-source records from the indexes.\\[3pt]
Proof sessions & \repolink{scripts/proof_workbench.py}{proof\_workbench.py} stores notes and submitted Lean probes, obtains verdicts from Lean, and binds a session claim to an accepted probe.\\[3pt]
Statement evidence & \repolink{scripts/paper_evidence.py}{paper\_evidence.py} locates each registered support at the recorded revision and checks its source and verification bindings; \repolink{scripts/paper_claim_evidence.py}{paper\_claim\_evidence.py} derives status and gap reports from those records.\\[3pt]
Editorial exchange & \repolink{scripts/short_paper_writer.py}{short\_paper\_writer.py} audits manuscripts and packages proposed revisions without applying or approving the return.\\[3pt]
Research history & \repolink{scripts/research_record.py}{research\_record.py} verifies the journal of entered returns and dispositions and reports the outstanding milestones of recorded outputs.\\[3pt]
Derived views & \repolink{scripts/refresh_projections.py}{refresh\_projections.py} runs builders in dependency order; \repolink{scripts/check_release.py}{check\_release.py} checks release contracts and freshness.\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{center}
A separate self-audit, \repolink{scripts/systems_paper_evidence.py}{systems\_paper\_evidence.py}, checks this systems manuscript's text and cited source bindings. These are implemented interfaces, not reports that every operation has been executed successfully.
% END SENTENCE r8.architecture.tools

% SENTENCE r9.architecture.state
An optional proof session illustrates the boundary between producing evidence and adopting a result. It stores notes, exact Lean inputs, process-derived receipts and a closing outcome. Its claim command requires an accepted probe and appends a session claim; it does not alter the reviewed public claim registry. The journal separately checks the sequence and hash chain of entered returns and dispositions. Later work can therefore inspect recorded inputs and decisions without the original conversation.
% END SENTENCE r9.architecture.state

% SENTENCE r8.architecture.roles
\subsection{Responsibilities and adoption}
A researcher chooses the question and the evidence needed to answer it. An agent can inspect files, run tools and prepare a change under the public instructions; a contributor can also send an ordinary argument or explanation without a clone or an agent. The maintainer reviews scope, attribution and unresolved obligations before adoption. These are responsibilities, not necessarily different people or agents: contributor and reviewer may coincide. The \repolink{docs/agents/README.md}{agent quickstart} and \repolink{CONTRIBUTING.md}{contribution guide} describe setup and review.
% END SENTENCE r8.architecture.roles

% SENTENCE r8.architecture.iteration
An iteration retrieves relevant work, investigates a question and returns an argument, experiment, correction or manuscript change with its evidence and limits. Review can adopt, revise, defer or reject the proposal. Accepted changes update the authored records; builders regenerate dependent views and release checks test consistency. Structured returns explicitly entered into the journal retain their dispositions. Ordinary issues and pull requests can reach review without a journal session (Section~\ref{sec:contribute}).
% END SENTENCE r8.architecture.iteration

\section{Worked case: reviewing an explanation}\label{sec:example}\label{sec:predigestion}


% SENTENCE r8.case.system-role
The worked case comes from Erd\H{o}s Problem~257, which asks whether every infinite subseries of $1+1/3+1/7+1/15+\cdots$ is irrational. The theorem used here proves irrationality under a weighted summability condition on the retained exponents, with the same conclusion for every infinite subset and every integer base at least two. Dropping that condition would claim the unresolved general case. Appendix~\ref{app:worked-proof} introduces the series, its antecedents and the proof.
% END SENTENCE r8.case.system-role

% SENTENCE r8.case.proof-role
Consider a contributor revising that explanation. The coverage row \texttt{res:weighted-support} in \repolink{docs/paper_lean_coverage.json}{paper\_lean\_coverage.json} fixes the printed statement and lists two Lean supports. The explanation here has a separate \repolink{docs/systems_paper_sentences.json}{passage record}, citing the ordinary proof and a formal declaration. The claim-evidence builder derives status or gap reports; the passage checker tests text and source bindings.

Neither Lean proof need change when the explanation loses its weighted hypothesis. The prose edit makes its passage binding stale; rebinding can remove that warning without repairing the claim. Review must compare the wording with the cited statements. Accepted edits update the explanation and its record before publication views are regenerated. Figure~\ref{fig:hypothesis} compares the three versions. This is an illustration, not a new test run.
% END SENTENCE r8.case.proof-role

% SENTENCE r15.fig.hypothesis
\begin{figure}[htbp]\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}
